Here's how to collect the assembly-loading trace on your Linux VM:

### 1. Enable the Assembly Loader diagnostic event source

Set these environment variables before launching your app:

```bash
export DOTNET_DiagnosticPorts=""
export COMPlus_AssemblyLoader=1          # legacy knob (still works)
# or the modern equivalent:
export DOTNET_EnableDiagnostics=1
```

### 2. Collect a Fusion-style trace with `dotnet-trace`

```bash
# Install the tool (once)
dotnet tool install -g dotnet-trace

# Collect loader events
dotnet-trace collect \
  --providers Microsoft-Windows-DotNETRuntime:0x4:4 \
  -- dotnet ./YourApp.dll
```

`0x4` is the **AssemblyLoader** keyword; `:4` is Informational verbosity. The output `.nettrace` file can be opened in **PerfView** (Windows) or converted:

```bash
dotnet-trace convert trace.nettrace --format speedscope
```

### 3. Get detailed text logging (simplest approach)

```bash
export COREHOST_TRACE=1
export COREHOST_TRACEFILE=host_trace.log
dotnet ./YourApp.dll
```

This writes the full host/resolver probe log to `host_trace.log` — every path the runtime tried when resolving each assembly.

### 4. Inspect the exception itself

`ReflectionTypeLoadException` carries a `LoaderExceptions` array with the **real** failures. Make sure you're logging it:

```csharp
try
{
    var types = assembly.GetTypes();
}
catch (ReflectionTypeLoadException ex)
{
    foreach (var loaderEx in ex.LoaderExceptions)
        Console.Error.WriteLine(loaderEx);
}
```

### 5. Common causes with custom `AssemblyLoadContext`

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---|---|
| `FileNotFoundException` in `LoaderExceptions` | Dependency not in plugin directory; override `Load()` to probe there |
| `FileLoadException` / version mismatch | Plugin built against a different version of a shared dep; use `AssemblyDependencyResolver` |
| Native library `DllNotFoundException` | Missing `runtimes/linux-x64/native/` layout; override `LoadUnmanagedDll()` |

### Recommended minimal `AssemblyLoadContext`

```csharp
class PluginLoadContext : AssemblyLoadContext
{
    private readonly AssemblyDependencyResolver _resolver;

    public PluginLoadContext(string pluginPath) : base(isCollectible: true)
    {
        _resolver = new AssemblyDependencyResolver(pluginPath);
    }

    protected override Assembly? Load(AssemblyName name)
    {
        var path = _resolver.ResolveAssemblyToPath(name);
        return path != null ? LoadFromAssemblyPath(path) : null;
    }

    protected override IntPtr LoadUnmanagedDll(string unmanagedDllName)
    {
        var path = _resolver.ResolveUnmanagedDllToPath(unmanagedDllName);
        return path != null ? LoadUnmanagedDllFromPath(path) : IntPtr.Zero;
    }
}
```

Start with **step 4** (read `LoaderExceptions`) — it usually points straight to the missing or mismatched assembly. Use **step 3** (`COREHOST_TRACE`) if you need to see every probing path the runtime checked.
